From e2b7e82b7f90229a36a3d15b7d23f223d68ec6a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Colliers <mail@thomascolliers.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 22:37:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] media: qcom: camss: Add CSIPHY v2.2.1 (milos) lane config

Add the D-PHY lane register sequence and AFE tuning for a 560 MHz link
frequency, corresponding to 1.12 Gbps per lane, for the CSIPHY v2.2.1
revision on milos. The settings are transcribed from the downstream
cam_csiphy_2_2_1_hwreg.h.

The sequence selects four-lane, two-phase D-PHY mode and programs the
v2.2.1 common registers and per-lane tuning. The common-control register
window starts at offset 0x1000, allowing the generic common-control
writes in csiphy_lanes_enable() to address the correct registers. The
data-rate-specific AFE/CDR settings use the standard-channel values;
duplicate short-channel settings are omitted. The table includes both
bytes of the settle count, so extend the existing runtime substitution
to program the high byte as well. As with the other gen2 PHYs,
skew-calibration entries are not applied.

Assisted-by: pi:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Thomas Colliers <mail@thomascolliers.com>
---
